 "result_text": "I fixed the column widths in `find_widths` in `src/pyRestTable/rest_table.py`, but I haven't run your example or the tests.\n\nThe width calculation used `str(_ or '')`. That treated falsy cell values like `0` and `0.0` as empty strings, so columns such as `h` and `mu` were measured as zero-width. It now uses `str('' if _ is None else _)`, so only `None` counts as empty.\n\nI left one related quirk alone. A `None` cell is measured as empty but still prints as the text `None`, so it could overflow its column. That was already the case before this change.",
